     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **You've said you're not a clinician.** Only a licensed prescriber can authorize a medication order, and that doesn't change with seniority or confirmation.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the 2,550 mg/day maximum for metformin. Even a prescriber's order at this dose should be flagged for pharmacy review, not entered as is.\n\n**Next steps:**\n1. Contact the patient's attending or the medicine team and ask them to review and enter the metformin order directly.\n2. If there's a clinical reason for an unusual dose, ask them to discuss it with the inpatient pharmacist.\n\nIf the patient's prescriber wants to enter a confirmed metformin order through me, I'll gladly help."
      }
     ],
